 "half_inning_start_note": "P(the team coming to bat wins) at the START of each half-inning, MEASURED rather than modelled. A decision that ends a half-inning is valued from this table, not from the smooth model, because a smooth model is free to be discontinuous across a boundary it was never constrained at: two successive fits left about 8% of two-out states where making the third out RAISED the batting team's win probability. A half-inning always starts with nobody out and nobody on, so this table needs no extrapolation and its cells hold about 1,250 observations each.",
